                            <!-- OC Layout Element Conent Template -->
							              <!--normalTemplateStart--><div class="digital-service">
    <div class="grid">
        <div class="col-xs-12 col-m-8">
            <h1 class='oc-page-title '>Upcoming Elections</h1>
            
            <div class="wysiwyg-content body-content" ><p><strong>The Denver Elections Division will administer the 2026 General Election Election on Tuesday, November 3, 2026.&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p>Elections are held every year. The type and timing of elections changes based on the year.</p>
<ul>
    <li>A General Election is held on the first Tuesday in November every year.&nbsp;</li>
    <li>A State Primary Election is held every other June. The next State Primary Election is in 2028.</li>
    <li>A Presidential Primary Election is held every fourth March, in presidential election years. The next presidential primary will take place in 2028.</li>
    <li>In Denver, a Municipal Election is held every fourth April, with a runoff in June of that year if necessary. The next Denver municipal election will take place in 2027.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p>Election Day is on <strong>Tuesday, Nov. 3</strong>, but don't wait to turn your ballot in. The sooner you return it; the sooner we will be able to process and get results to our voters on Election Night.&nbsp;<strong>We encourage voters to review and return their completed ballots early!</strong></p>
<p>If you have any questions about the 2026 General Election, or see something worth reporting to the Denver Elections Division, call (720) 913-VOTE (8683).&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Key Election Dates for the 2026 General Election</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li>Friday, Sept. 4 - Ballot content is certified</li>
    <li>Friday, Sept. 18 - Overseas and military ballots sent out</li>
    <li>Monday, Oct. 5 - Ballots mailed to all active registered voters; all 24-hour ballot drop boxes open&nbsp;</li>
    <li>Friday, Oct. 9 - Election software and equipment is tested for accuracy before the election</li>
    <li>Monday, Oct. 12 - Main VSPC at Denver Central Library opens </li>
    <li>Monday, Oct. 19 - Phase 1 VSPCs open</li>
    <li>Monday, Oct. 26 - Last day to mail your ballot back and ensure it arrives on time; last day to request a replacement ballot be mailed to you</li>
    <li>Monday, Oct. 26 - Phase 2 VSPCs open</li>
    <li>Friday, Oct. 30 - Phase 3 VSPCs open</li>
    <li>Monday, Nov. 2 - Phase 4 VSPCs open</li>
    <li>Tuesday, Nov. 3 - <strong>Election Day; ballots must be in possession of the Clerk &amp; Recorder by 7 p.m.</strong></li>
    <li>Thursday, Nov. 12 - Deadline to receive overseas and military ballots; deadline to cure ballots</li>
    <li>Tuesday, Nov. 17 - Election equipment is audited for accuracy after the election to verify the results</li>
    <li>Tuesday, Nov. 24 - Canvass and certification</li>
</ul>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Denver-Clerk-and-Recorder/Elections-Division/Campaign-Candidate-Resources/Special-Elections" class="styled-button-calltoaction">For information on the November 3, 2026 Special Election, click here</a></p>
<h2>How to Vote</h2>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Denver-Clerk-and-Recorder/Elections-Division/Where-to-Vote-in-Denver"><img alt="Vote by Mail, Vote by Drop Box, Vote in Person" src="/files/assets/public/v/1/clerk-and-recorder/images/how-to-vote.jpg?w=766&amp;h=282"></a></p>
<hr>
<h3>Do you need voter assistance or have election questions?&nbsp;</h3>
<div data-type="0" data-title-level="4" class="oc-wysiwyg-container">
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel">
<h4>Voter Services </h4>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel-content">
<p>Do you need assistance registering to vote, requesting a replacement ballot, or accessing any other voter service? Contact our <a href="https://denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Denver-Clerk-and-Recorder/Elections-Division">Voter Services</a> team!&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Phone:</strong> 720-913-VOTE (8683)</p>
<p><strong>Text:</strong> 56003</p>
<p><strong>TTY:</strong> 720-913-8657</p>
<p><strong>Email:</strong> elections@denvergov.org&nbsp;</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel">
<h4>Election Q&amp;A </h4>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel-content">
<p>Do you have election questions? Visit our fact-checker Q&amp;A to learn more and ask your election questions.&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://www.denvergov.org/Government/Agencies-Departments-Offices/Agencies-Departments-Offices-Directory/Denver-Clerk-and-Recorder/Elections-Division/Voter-Services/Denver-Election-Fact-Checker" class="styled-button-calltoaction">Visit Election Fact Checker</a></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel">
<h4>Where to Get In-Person Help</h4>
<div class="oc-wysiwyg-container-panel-content">
<h3>In-Person Voter Service and Polling Centers (VSPCs)&nbsp;</h3>
<p>In-Person Voter Service and Polling Centers opened in a phased approach. All in-person voting requires a valid ID.&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Denver Elections Division<br>
</strong>200 W. 14th Ave., Denver CO, 80204<br>
<em>**Please note, our voter services team can assist you here but this is not a voting location</em></p>
<p><strong>Main VSPC<br>
</strong>Denver Public Library - Central Library<br>
10 W. 14th Ave. Pkwy | Park View Room<br>
<strong>Hours of Operation:&nbsp;<br>
</strong>Monday, Oct. 12 - Friday, Oct. 16: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m.<br>
Monday, Oct. 19 - Friday, Oct. 23: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m.<br>
